1
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:08,960
- Cheers.     - Cheers.

2
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:13,590
You look cute in bubbles.

3
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:15,470
Ahh, you're just all liquored up.

4
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:21,430
Hey, it's me. I'm coming in.

5
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,940
I've had a very long, hard day.

6
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,070
Want some chicken?

7
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:35,320
No, thanks. No chicken. Bye-bye.

8
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,700
You sure? Some extra-crispy, dirty rice?

9
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:42,290
For the last time, no! Get out, Joey!

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:43,870
All right.

11
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:49,920
Are you okay? He wouldn't leave.

12
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:52,630
He kept asking me if I wanted chicken.

13
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,090
Chicken?

14
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:57,010
I could eat some chicken.

15
00:00:58,550 --> 00:00:59,970
Hey, Joe!

16
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:06,390
Could I get a, uh, three-piece, some coleslaw, some beans and a Coke?

17
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,940
Aah! Diet Coke.

18
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:52,360
- Hey.     - Hey.

19
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:55,230
- Morning, Pheebs.     - I have to tell you this story.

20
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:57,740
I was coming over and this cabdriver...

21
00:01:57,950 --> 00:01:59,030
Was his name Angus?

22
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:01,740
What?

23
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:04,200
He was a cabdriver we had in London.

24
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,990
Oh. Ha, ha, ha.

25
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,870
All right. Anyway...

26
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:10,370
What was that pub he took us to?

27
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,790
The Wheat Sheaf!

28
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,590
And they had that beer...

29
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:16,960
- Boddington's.     - Boddington's.

30
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:20,800
Ooh, uh, Pheebs was going to tell a story.

31
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:23,720
So he had a really funny hat.

32
00:02:23,970 --> 00:02:26,270
I don't want to talk about it.

33
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:29,850
- Hey.     - Hey, Ross!

34
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:32,020
Boddington's!

35
00:02:32,270 --> 00:02:33,730
Oh, man!

36
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:39,190
I'd walk back to London for another frosty one of those bad boys.

37
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:42,490
They have them at the British pub by the Trade Center.

38
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:44,160
Later!

39
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,740
Shouldn't Rachel be back?

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,500
Her plane got delayed.

41
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:50,540
But she should be here by now.

42
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:53,500
So you talked to her? Did she sound mad?

43
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,670
No. But she likes me.

44
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:58,760
You abandoned her on a plane to Greece.

45
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:01,880
I did not "abandon" Rachel. Okay?

46
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,010
Emily showed up at the airport.

47
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:07,310
I had to go after her. I did what I had to do.

48
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,020
She's my wife. Rachel is my wife.

49
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:11,440
Emily!

50
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:16,020
Emily is my wife.

51
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:18,570
Man, what is that?

52
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:21,490
You haven't heard from Emily?

53
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:23,780
Not since I lost her at the airport.

54
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:26,030
I can't believe she can outrun you.

55
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:28,740
Hey! She's fast, okay?

56
00:03:29,330 --> 00:03:32,960
You think you can beat me? Let's go! Outside!

57
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:36,460
Hi!

58
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,170
Hi! Rachel!

59
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:43,970
Rach, I am so sorry. I am so, so sorry.

60
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:46,760
Come on. You just did what you had to do.

61
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,100
Hi, Pheebs.

62
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:52,640
That's it? You're not mad? It must've been terrible.

63
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:54,940
Terrible? Hell, I was in Greece!

64
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:59,860
There was a nice hotel, nice beach, met the nice people.

65
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:02,320
It's not too shabby for Rachel.

66
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:07,030
So, what, that's it?

67
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:11,330
Well, yeah. We're cool. Totally cool.

68
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,830
Thanks, Rach. You're the best.

69
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:16,380
Oh, no. You're the best.

70
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:20,460
Oh, I got to go to the flower store.

71
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:24,050
No one will tell me where Emily is...

72
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:28,390
...so I'm sending 72 long-stemmed, red roses to her parents' house.

73
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,560
One for each day I've known and loved her.

74
00:04:31,770 --> 00:04:33,390
That should get her talking.

75
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:37,980
When you make out the card, be sure to make it out to "Emily."

76
00:04:42,610 --> 00:04:45,400
It's good that you had such a good time in Greece.

77
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:47,780
What?

78
00:04:49,410 --> 00:04:51,700
I didn't have a good time in Greece!

79
00:04:52,450 --> 00:04:54,660
Ross abandoned me!

80
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:59,080
I couldn't get a plane out. I had to stay in their suite!

81
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:04,260
People came up to me going, "Mrs. Geller! Why are you cry?"

82
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:07,970
I mean, it was so humiliating!

83
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:10,300
I felt like such an idiot!

84
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:12,810
It's all my fault. You know why?

85
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:16,440
Because I make very bad decisions.

86
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,850
Oh, that's not true.

87
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:21,570
Yes, it is true. I went after Ross in stupid London!

88
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:24,610
London is stupid! Stupid!

89
00:05:26,150 --> 00:05:28,070
I should've never gone to London.

90
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:31,990
From now on, you make all my decisions for me.

91
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,750
Oh, no. I did that for someone once.

92
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,920
I'm not comfortable having that power over someone's life.

93
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:40,540
I'll do it.

94
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:45,550
Fine. Monica, you are now in charge of my love life.

95
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,510
Okay. I got to go to work.

96
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:01,190
And, uh, Rachel, great to have you back.

97
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,320
Pheebs!

98
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:14,830
Always a pleasure.

99
00:06:21,330 --> 00:06:23,580

100
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:25,840
Rachel? Sweetie, look.

101
00:06:26,050 --> 00:06:28,510
Here's a cute picture of you and Joey.

102
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,010
He's married.

103
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:33,100
Ross is married. I still can't believe it.

104
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:36,060
Honey, sweetie, by the edges.

105
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:38,430
I'll just have to accept it.

106
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:40,270
I mean, it's my fault.

107
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:42,940
Edges! Fingers! Smudgy!

108
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:45,110
Oh, my God!

109
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:53,200
That's okay. I know that you're very upset right now.

110
00:06:53,410 --> 00:06:55,160
I know that wasn't about me.

111
00:06:55,490 --> 00:06:57,490
I bet it was about her a little.

112
00:06:57,950 --> 00:07:00,250
If you'd stop thinking about Ross...

113
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,330
...you'd notice there are great guys everywhere.

114
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:04,670
Look. Gunther.

115
00:07:07,550 --> 00:07:09,170
He's nice. He's cute.

116
00:07:09,670 --> 00:07:11,720
Yeah. I guess Gunther is...

117
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,970
What about that guy over there?

118
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:18,010
That's the guy you flirted with at the counter.

119
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:21,310
Oh, I don't know. I don't know.

120
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:22,640
You're going to talk to him.

121
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:26,440
I make your decisions, and I say you're going to talk to him.

122
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,570
All right.

123
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,950
You're the boss. I got to do what you tell me.

124
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,410
Say that to him, and you're golden.

125
00:07:37,950 --> 00:07:40,120
- Hey.     - Hey.

126
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:43,370
Hey, Pheebs. We got our pictures back from London.

127
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:46,290
Here's all of us at the Tower of London...

128
00:07:46,790 --> 00:07:48,380
Here we all are.

129
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:51,380
There's Ross and Joey and you and...

130
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:53,970
And me.

131
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:58,050
We've been talking about London too much.

132
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:01,350
Sorry, it's just because I couldn't be there.

133
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:05,060
All I get to do now is pregnant stuff. It bums me out.

134
00:08:05,310 --> 00:08:06,770
- I'm sorry.     - Sorry.

135
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:10,900
- What happened?     - A little of this, a little of that.

136
00:08:11,150 --> 00:08:12,820
I got myself a date tomorrow.

137
00:08:13,070 --> 00:08:17,070
See? Didn't I tell you? You're getting over Ross already.

138
00:08:18,660 --> 00:08:19,700
Get out.

139
00:08:19,870 --> 00:08:22,200

140
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,760
What took so long?

141
00:08:37,010 --> 00:08:40,310
I got caught up at work. But I'm quitting tomorrow.

142
00:08:45,350 --> 00:08:47,560
So thanks for having me over.

143
00:08:50,230 --> 00:08:51,270
Rach...

144
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,570
Pheebs...

145
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:07,080
See you, man.

146
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:11,880
What the hell was that?

147
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:16,720
Probably some European goodbye thing he picked up in London.

148
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:18,550
That's not European.

149
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:20,970
It felt French.

150
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,980
I really had a good time.

151
00:09:28,230 --> 00:09:29,600
Yeah, me too.

152
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:32,900
- So...     - So...

153
00:09:33,150 --> 00:09:34,230
I guess this is it.

154
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,030
Yeah, um...

155
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:39,820
- Unless you want to come inside?     - Yeah!

156
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:45,250
Oh, uh, wait a minute. You know what? I can't decide this.

157
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:49,580
Okay. Just hold on a second.

158
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,630
Um, hi.

159
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,090
Hi.

160
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:58,630
Where's Monica? I have to ask her something.

161
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,260
Doing her laundry.

162
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,100
What's that?

163
00:10:02,850 --> 00:10:04,970
It came in the mail today.

164
00:10:06,310 --> 00:10:08,730
It's 72 long-stemmed, red roses.

165
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:11,860
One for each day I've known and loved Emily...

166
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:14,230
...cut up into mulch.

167
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,990
Honey, that's awful.

168
00:10:19,070 --> 00:10:20,110
It's not so bad.

169
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,700
Monica's going to make potpourri.

170
00:10:25,870 --> 00:10:30,210
I think I'm going to go wander out in the rain for a while.

171
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:31,460
It's not raining.

172
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:34,210
I can't catch a break.

173
00:10:35,630 --> 00:10:38,880
You're not going anywhere. Sit right here.

174
00:10:39,130 --> 00:10:42,220
I'll make you some tea and we'll talk this out.

175
00:10:42,470 --> 00:10:43,550
All right?

176
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,760
Okay.

177
00:10:47,390 --> 00:10:48,560
- Hey, Dave.     - Yeah.

178
00:10:48,730 --> 00:10:53,400
Um, I need to take a rain check. My roommate is really sick.

179
00:10:53,610 --> 00:10:54,650
Okay. Bye.

180
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,860
Honey, listen.

181
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:03,740
I know things seem so bad...

182
00:11:03,950 --> 00:11:06,280
...and that they won't get any...

183
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:08,370
Could I talk to you?

184
00:11:09,790 --> 00:11:11,370
I dropped some socks.

185
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,670
Yeah.

186
00:11:21,050 --> 00:11:25,760
What is the matter with you? Do you want to fall into the trap?

187
00:11:25,970 --> 00:11:28,810
You did not drop any socks!

188
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:31,180
I saw Dave, and he said you blew him off!

189
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:32,480
You listen to me!

190
00:11:32,690 --> 00:11:36,560
I'm calling the shots! I say you leave Ross and go get Dave.

191
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:37,940
What are you doing?

192
00:11:38,150 --> 00:11:42,150
Well, ultimately I was trying, you know, I wanted...

193
00:11:42,990 --> 00:11:45,620
...to tell him that I'm still in love with him.

194
00:11:45,950 --> 00:11:48,990
What? You cannot tell him that!

195
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,580
Why? Why not?

196
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:52,870
People love to hear that!

197
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:56,580
I make the decisions and I say no!

198
00:11:56,790 --> 00:12:00,420
You know what? No, you don't make my decisions, because...

199
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:02,090
...you're fired.

200
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,090
You can't fire me.

201
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:08,850
I make your decisions, and I say I'm not fired. Ha!

202
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,270
Well...

203
00:12:21,820 --> 00:12:23,990
Rachel! Come on, let me in!

204
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:25,740
Having some trouble?

205
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:28,280
Rachel locked the door.

206
00:12:28,490 --> 00:12:31,490
I'll kick that door in if you give me some sugar.

207
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:38,710
Rachel! Let me in!

208
00:12:46,890 --> 00:12:47,970
Thank you.

209
00:12:50,890 --> 00:12:53,520
Rachel? Can I talk to you outside for a sec?

210
00:12:54,060 --> 00:12:55,140
No.

211
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:57,940
We really need to talk.

212
00:12:58,230 --> 00:12:59,650
Well, then talk.

213
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,940
Okay, I will.

214
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:07,700
Remember that thing we just discussed that you wanted to do?

215
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,120
Yes.

216
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:10,490
What thing?

217
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:16,750
Rachel wants to take swing dance lessons.

218
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:19,920
Which I think is a really stupid idea.

219
00:13:20,170 --> 00:13:23,250
It's dangerous. She won't get what she wants.

220
00:13:23,510 --> 00:13:26,510
And who knows who she might end up hurting?

221
00:13:32,810 --> 00:13:36,230
Monica's right. Swing dancing can be tricky.

222
00:13:38,310 --> 00:13:39,600
I have to use the phone.

223
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:43,780
I got to cancel those five, giant teddy bears I sent to Emily.

224
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:46,490
My God. Think of the massacre.

225
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:48,780
I'm going to do it.

226
00:13:49,030 --> 00:13:50,820
I know you think I'm crazy.

227
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:54,160
But before you tell him, try to find one person...

228
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:56,700
...who thinks it's a good idea. I bet you can't.

229
00:13:56,910 --> 00:13:58,000
Please?

230
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:01,540
All right. Fine.

231
00:14:06,050 --> 00:14:07,920
Joey! I'm in!

232
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:10,300
All right. Good deal.

233
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:18,890
Pheebs! Hey!

234
00:14:19,810 --> 00:14:23,360
Uh, Pheebs?  Yeah?

235
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:27,820
Um, you know how you were saying you didn't get to go to London...

236
00:14:28,070 --> 00:14:29,860
...and you were feeling left out?     - Yeah.

237
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:32,950
Well, we all felt really bad about that...

238
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:36,620
...so we decided to take a little trip together.

239
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:39,000
Oh, that's so nice!

240
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:41,040
How great! Where's the trip?

241
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:44,790
- Well, we thought we would all go to a picnic...

242
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:48,880
...in Central Park!     - Central Park?

243
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,260
All of us. All day.

244
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,840
That sucks!

245
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:56,510
That's not a trip! I just came from there.

246
00:14:56,850 --> 00:14:59,730
What'll we high-five about at the stupid park?

247
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:02,900
It's right by my house. All right!

248
00:15:04,730 --> 00:15:08,690
I'm going home to bask in the triumph of my Central Park idea.

249
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,950
Hold on a sec there, Mr. Kissy.

250
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:15,490
I wanted to talk to you about...

251
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:18,870
...this whole new European thing you've got going on.

252
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:22,250
And I need to say it makes me very uncomfortable...

253
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,960
...and I just, you know, just stop it!

254
00:15:26,170 --> 00:15:28,670
Just bringing some culture to the group.

255
00:15:29,010 --> 00:15:31,760
That's fine. Just don't bring it in my mouth.

256
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:34,260
It makes me want to puke.

257
00:15:41,270 --> 00:15:43,600
Hey, everybody! Pheebs is here!

258
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:48,690
Phoebe! Whoo!  Okay. Whoo! Hi!

259
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:53,660
Pheebs, we decided that the picnic idea was a little...

260
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:56,240
It didn't have any... Well, it blew.

261
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:03,210
We thought that this afternoon we'd all go away for the whole weekend...

262
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,710
...to Atlantic City.

263
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:09,380
Ooh, Atlantic City! Oh, that's a great plan! Whose plan was that?

264
00:16:09,590 --> 00:16:10,670
Mine!

265
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:14,550
- Wait. It was my plan.     - No...

266
